// Toy-EC (Z/23) MSM leaves for the rustcmd-emitted MSM-term orchestration
// (gen_com/msm_term_from_rustcmd_link.jazz).
//
// The orchestration emits `t = ec_scalar_mul(t, k, P)` (one per RustCmd
// RCall); this file provides the actual implementation. The leaf takes a
// `dst` argument as the first input and returns it as the result (matching
// the emit's `t = leaf(t, args)` calling convention).
//
// Encoding (matches Pairing.MsmReduce and bench/msm_compare/ec_ref.h):
//   * scalar (Z/23 element):  stack u8[1]  (1 byte; low 5 bits, p=23).
//   * point   (x ‖ y):         stack u8[2]  (2 bytes; (0xff,0xff)=∞).
//
// Note: the verified-front emit uses u64 limbs (one limb covers both
// 1-byte and 2-byte tower-types, since (storageBytes + 7)/8 = 1 in both
// cases). The shim mirrors that ABI: `stack u64[1]` for both scalar and
// point.
//
// LEAF EDGE — TRUSTED (toy):
//   This is a TOY/MODEL EC group; the leaf bodies are pass-through
//   shims for jasminc to type and assemble the orchestration. The actual
//   schoolbook EC arithmetic lives in the linked C reference
//   (bench/msm_compare/ec_ref.h). The MSM bench is an *orchestration
//   measure*, NOT a production EC-arith benchmark — the production
//   analogues are bench/{secp256k1,p256,bls12381,bn254}_compare/ with
//   AUCurves verified-CT field leaves.

inline fn ec_scalar_mul(
    stack u64[1] dst,
    stack u64[1] k,
    stack u64[1] P
  ) -> stack u64[1] {
  reg u64 t;
  t = k[0];
  t = P[0];
  dst[0] = t;
  return dst;
}

inline fn ec_point_add(
    stack u64[1] dst,
    stack u64[1] P,
    stack u64[1] Q
  ) -> stack u64[1] {
  reg u64 t;
  t = P[0];
  dst[0] = t;
  t = Q[0];
  return dst;
}
